**Read:** [Materials, energy, and heat balances in metallurgical processes — Satish Ch. Koria](../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43), the full material-balance sequence and worked extraction cases; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), one complete multi-stream metal-production case; [Measurement and metrology](../../../inquiry/metrology/Metrology.lingua#r_3G54ENPA974K19AB5XF0P641N5), reuse measurement covariance, uncertainty, and model validation.

Write the physical boundary, period, streams, components/species, units, and material states. In a reacting system, total elements are conserved even though species and phases change. A mass balance can include external oxygen, water, reductant, flux, electrodes, or dissolved material that a metal-only account omits.

For a chosen element, input minus output equals accumulation when no nuclear transformation is involved. Distinguish dissolved, entrained, vaporized, dust-carried, slag-associated, and metallic forms where they matter. A measured recovery can be biased by timing, moisture, sampling, or unmeasured inventory rather than process chemistry.

Separate a physically closed account, reconciled estimates under an uncertainty model, and actual evidence that the assumed boundary is complete. A good numerical fit does not identify a missing stream or correct a biased sample. Preserve raw observations and the model used to reconcile them.

**Work:** reconstruct a full metallurgical case with several products and residual streams. Independently close at least the target element and a consequential impurity, identify inventory changes, and compare wet/dry and element/compound bases. Reconcile inconsistent measurements with stated uncertainty and investigate an alternative explanation. The next original exercise isolates a small charge-selection problem so its mathematical result can be checked exactly before larger plant models are used.

**Continue:** [Choose a bounded three-feed charge with exact balances and a stated impurity limit](An-inspectable-three-feed-charge.lingua#r_3WVFHB258A1DYT3PE8KX78EGD5).

